{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-bring-cone-tetraplectic-structure","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:bring-cone-tetraplectic-structure","kind":"definition","title":"Tetraplectic structure on the affine cone $C(\\mathcal{B})$ over Bring's curve","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-brings-surface"],"cites":["references/foth2002"],"tags":["tetraplectic","bring-cone","s5-symmetry","invariant-volume-form","young-diagram","archimedean-universe"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Tetraplectic.BringCone","sorryFree":true,"text":"bring-cone-tetraplectic-structure.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:bring-cone-tetraplectic-structure\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{B} \\subset \\mathbb{P}^4</code> be\n<a href=\"#def:brings-surface\" data-at=\"brings-surface/brings-surface-qou\">Bring's surface</a>. Its <strong>affine cone</strong> is the affine variety</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  C(\\mathcal{B})\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\Bigl\\{\\, x \\in \\mathbb{C}^5 \\;:\\;\n    \\textstyle\\sum_j x_j = \\sum_j x_j^2 = \\sum_j x_j^3 = 0 \\,\\Bigr\\}\n  \\;\\subset\\; \\mathbb{C}^5,</code></pre>\n<p>a complex surface, hence a real <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code>-manifold. Write <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M = C(\\mathcal{B})</code>.</p>\n<p>On a <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4m</code>-dimensional manifold, a <strong>tetraplectic structure</strong> <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"foth2002\">[foth2002]</span>\nis a closed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code>-form <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega \\in \\Omega^4(M)</code> whose <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m</code>-th power <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega^m</code> is\na non-degenerate volume form.</p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S_5 \\times \\mathbb{Z}_2</code> act on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M</code> by the discrete symmetries of\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{B}</code>, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}_2</code> generated by an involution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tau</code>, and let\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\omega_0</code> be a volume form on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M</code>. The <strong>tetraplectic structure on\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C(\\mathcal{B})</code></strong> is the averaged form</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Omega\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\frac{1}{|S_5|} \\sum_{g \\in S_5}\n    \\bigl( \\omega_0 \\pm \\tau^{*}(g^{*}\\omega_0) \\bigr),</code></pre>\n<p>and the associated <strong>state space</strong> is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H} = L^2(M, \\Omega)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/bring-cone-tetraplectic-structure.md","heading":"Definition","number":"8.8.5","page":"b/def-bring-cone-tetraplectic-structure","qa":{"counts":{"pass":39,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":52}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Tetraplectic.BringCone","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/BringCone.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
